-- Source: "CCMAS_ELS Undergraduate Handbook.pdf" (department handbook, 42 pages).
-- 107 rows from the Standard FOUR-YEAR programme (full timetable: ELS/LIN major
-- courses, both stress areas, GST/ENT/FAC/GSP/COS ancillary courses and the
-- two-unit language electives). The three-year direct-entry programme and the
-- Combined Honours tracks (English/History, /Theatre and Film Studies, /French,
-- /German) are not loaded here.
--
-- ADDITIVE ONLY: nothing is deleted or renamed. The department's earlier
-- website-based rows stay exactly as they are. Re-running this file is safe
-- (a row is inserted only if the same code + title + level is not there yet).
--
-- "UNN-" prefixes in the handbook are dropped (UNN-ELS 111 -> ELS 111,
-- UNN-GSP 105 -> GSP 105, UNN-COS 101 -> COS 101, UNN-IGB 101 -> IGB 101).
-- Codes follow the programme tables, with these handbook inconsistencies:
--   * ELS 103 carries 3 units in the four-year table (its description heading
--     says 2); the table is used.
--   * Folklore in African Literature I is ELS 337 in the table but headed
--     ELS 339 in the descriptions; ELS 337 is used.
--   * ELS 222's description cites "ELS 223"; read as ELS 221 (Phonetics I).
--   * UNN-ELS 436 is titled "American Literature Survey: The Beginnings to the
--     Modern Period" in the table and "...to the Romantic Movement" in its
--     description; the table title is used.
--   * ENT 312 (Venture Creation) is used for the four-year 300L second semester.
--   * COS 304 Computer Applications sits at 200L second semester per the table.
-- Stress-area courses are tagged in the description; electives set is_elective.
-- Ancillary courses have no descriptions in this handbook; they borrow real
-- descriptions from existing rows with the same code (bottom of file).
-- =============================================================================

with src (course_code, course_title, level, semester, credit_units, description, topics, is_elective) as (
values
  ('GST 111', 'Communication in English I', '100 Level', 'first', 1, '', '[]'::jsonb, false),
  ('LIN 101', 'Introduction to Linguistics', '100 Level', 'first', 2, '', '[]'::jsonb, false),
  ('ELS 101', 'A Survey of the English Language', '100 Level', 'first', 2, 'This seeks to introduce students to the fundamentals of the major sub-disciplines in English such as morphology and syntax, phonetics (phonology), stylistics and semantics, etc.', '["This seeks to introduce students to the fundamentals of the major sub-disciplines in English such as morphology and syntax, phonetics (phonology), stylistics and semantics, etc"]'::jsonb, false),
  ('ELS 103', 'Introduction to English Grammar and Composition', '100 Level', 'first', 3, 'This course introduces basic elements of Grammar to acquaint the students with the parts of speech in English, the demands of concord and tense in producing grammatical and acceptable sentences. Basic composition, letter writing, and controlled expression methods are also taught.', '["This course introduces basic elements of Grammar to acquaint the students with the parts of speech in English, the demands of concord and tense in producing grammatical and acceptable sentences","Basic composition, letter writing, and controlled expression methods are also taught"]'::jsonb, false),
  ('ELS 115', 'Introduction to Prose Literature', '100 Level', 'first', 2, 'The aim is to introduce the student to literary language and to the organising principles or techniques of fiction through selected short stories and novels. Basic elements of fiction will be defined and illustrated from chosen texts to show how these cohere to yield the given text. This course is a prerequisite for ELS 235, ELS 335, and ELS 433.', '["The aim is to introduce the student to literary language and to the organising principles or techniques of fiction through selected short stories and novels","Basic elements of fiction will be defined and illustrated from chosen texts to show how these cohere to yield the given text","This course is a prerequisite for ELS 235, ELS 335, and ELS 433"]'::jsonb, false),
  ('ELS 111', 'Basic Literary Concepts', '100 Level', 'first', 2, 'This course presents the basic issues of the study of literature: what is literary art? The concepts of myth, fable, story, and sequence; the forms of literature; the concept of representation/mimesis; action and modes of action; myth-making; the voices marking the different forms: the narrator in narrative, the speaker in lyric, and the character in drama.', '["This course presents the basic issues of the study of literature: what is literary art?","The concepts of myth, fable, story, and sequence","The forms of literature","The concept of representation/mimesis","Action and modes of action","Myth-making","The voices marking the different forms: the narrator in narrative, the speaker in lyric, and the character in drama"]'::jsonb, false),
  ('GSP 105', 'Introduction to Natural Science I', '100 Level', 'first', 1, '', '[]'::jsonb, false),
  ('COS 101', 'Introduction to Computer Science', '100 Level', 'first', 2, '', '[]'::jsonb, false),
